#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE Retryable pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Content-addressed, deterministic stages that hand off through storage and can retry while the database is down."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Layer L3 · domain: product · depends on: [CAP-ORCHESTRATION]{1}, [CAP-STORAGE]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Build processing stages that can be retried, overlapped and re-run without being wrong."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Delivery is at-least-once; content addressing makes overlap wasteful instead of wrong ([P8]{1}, [P9]{2}). Keeping the database out of every stage but one lets the rest retry through a database outage."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Storage folders as hand-off points; one job per stage."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "A provenance record per item."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "A stage that keeps an index in memory must run with concurrency one, or concurrent runs miss matches across each other silently."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "An input's identity is the hash of its bytes; duplicates and re-deliveries converge on one record.{1}*Example:* The same scanned page uploaded as scan1.pdf and as register-final.pdf has the same hash, so only one record results."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Submit the same file twice under different names; one record results."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "The same input produces byte-identical output; any randomness is seeded per item from a hash of stable keys."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Process a fixed corpus twice; outputs are byte-identical."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Each stage is its own job, triggered by the output of the stage before it, so no stage can outrun its predecessor."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "The job graph has one job per stage with storage-arrival triggers."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Pending work is recomputed from what exists, never consumed from a queue on read, so a failed run strands nothing."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Kill a run mid-way; the next run processes the remainder."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Writes are atomic (write to a temporary name, then move), so a reader never sees a partial output."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Code review and a fault-injection test find no partial files."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Only the publishing stage connects to the operational database; every other stage can retry while it is unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "With the database unreachable, upstream stages complete."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "CAP-PIPELINE.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Each item carries a provenance record of every stage that touched it, with versions; a missing stage reads as absent, never invented."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-pipeline.md
msgid "Every published item has a provenance record with a field per stage."
msgstr ""

